# Build context exclusions: no version control, local state, tooling, downloads or secrets.
# The image copies only requirements/h1.lock, src/, the baked grid snapshot and the signed
# permission registry under docs/work/permissions/; this file keeps everything else out of the
# context so nothing credential-shaped can leak in through a later COPY or ADD.
#
# build/grid-data/ is deliberately NOT listed: the Dockerfile copies the grid replay snapshot
# GRID-1 bakes with scripts/grid/build_data.py from the context into the image. That data is
# company WESM data — it is excluded from the public export by scripts/release/allowlist.json
# and never committed, and it ships inside the deployed image only. ATG-8: the one COPY line
# carries the whole directory, so ATG-4's `catalog.json`, ATG-5's `briefs.json` and
# `findings.json` and ATG-7's `assets/` profiles travel with the seven GRID-1 files and need
# no line of their own — listing any of them here would keep a served file out of the image.
#
# build/hosting/ (PERF-5) IS listed: it is the stage scripts/deploy/stage_hosting.py assembles
# for Firebase Hosting out of build/grid-data and src/grid. It is a second copy of the same
# files, published from the repository tree, and no Dockerfile line reads it. build/firebase.json
# is the generated Hosting config the stager writes beside that stage — a deploy artifact the
# image never reads either.
build/hosting
build/firebase.json
.git
.gitignore
.gitattributes
.local
.github
.codex
.claude
.meos
.agents
**/node_modules
node_modules
__pycache__
**/__pycache__
**/*.py[cod]
.venv
venv
*.egg-info
.pytest_cache
.mypy_cache
.ruff_cache
docs
# …except the signed permission records the image copies (Dockerfile): a real record must cite a
# permission the registry holds, and without this line the COPY source is outside the context.
!docs/work/permissions
tests
experiments
archive
ideas
poc
